%% PLANNED sequence view, written from the ADRs before any real run.
%% The assignment needs a sequence view of ONE REAL RUN. Replace this file with
%% sequence_view.mmd once a real run exists, using its real run IDs, PR number and timings.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor M as Maintainer
    participant GH as GitHub (issue / PR)
    participant O as Job 1 Orchestrator
    participant RA as Requirements agent<br/>gemini-3.5-flash-lite
    participant J as Testability judge<br/>gemini-3.8-flash
    participant DI as Design + impl agent<br/>gemini-3.8-flash
    participant TA as Testing agent<br/>gemini-3.6-flash
    participant A as Artifacts (state.json, outputs)
    participant R as Job 2 Release (script)
    participant CI as ci.yml
    participant RV as Job 3 Review<br/>reviewer gemini-4-hydrogen
    participant RT as Job 4 Route (script)

    M->>GH: add label "autose" to issue #n
    GH->>O: issues: labeled (concurrency group autose-n)
    O->>A: download latest autose-issue-n (if any), else new state.json + baseline.json + issue snapshot
    O->>O: done flag set? → comment and exit · issue edited since snapshot? → stop
    O->>O: start at target stage if set, else last passed stage
    O->>GH: issue mirror comment: stage 1

    O->>RA: issue snapshot (random delimiter, untrusted), A1 skill, repo
    RA-->>O: spec.json, attempt_summary.md (or rejected.json if very vague: run stops, Route comments reason + questions)
    O->>O: G1 schema check
    O->>J: acceptance_criteria only
    J-->>O: judge.json (all testable)
    O->>GH: post assumptions comment (only if vague)

    O->>DI: issue snapshot, spec.json, ARCHITECTURE.md, repo
    DI-->>O: design.json
    O->>O: G2 EXISTING / NEW check
    O->>DI: continue same conversation: implement
    DI-->>O: working-tree changes, attempt_summary.md
    O->>O: git diff → diff.patch, G3 install/import, ruff, scope guard

    O->>TA: phase 1: issue, ACs, interface list, clean-commit copy
    TA-->>O: tests/test_ac<n>_*
    O->>TA: phase 2: own tests in copy with implementation
    TA-->>O: setup fixes only, attempt_summary.md
    O->>O: G4 pytest vs baseline.json, AC coverage, asserts unchanged → test_report.md
    O->>A: upload artifacts + state.json (last passed: 4)

    O->>R: needs: orchestrator
    R->>R: regex secret scan on diff
    R->>R: branch has foreign commits? → stop (never force-push)
    R->>GH: push autose/issue-n (PAT), open PR with minimal pr.md
    GH->>CI: PR / push event
    CI-->>R: green (polled ≤ 10 min)

    R->>RV: needs: release
    RV->>RV: run tests (sandbox container, no secrets)
    RV->>RV: reviewer agent in container: issue snapshot, diff, repo at PR HEAD (untrusted), test results
    RV->>RV: G6 evidence check on review.json
    RV->>GH: PR comment review.md + label

    RV->>RT: needs: review (if: always())
    RT->>A: read state.json (round)
    alt approved, or 2 rounds used
        RT->>A: mark state.json done
        RT->>GH: issue comment: ready for human decision
        M->>GH: merge or close (human)
    else changes requested (round < 2)
        RT->>A: write target stage (earliest classification), round + 1
        RT->>GH: workflow_dispatch(issue = n)
        Note over GH,O: new run starts at the target stage on the same branch and PR
    else any job failed, timed out or cancelled
        RT->>GH: stop comment linking the explanation artifact
    end
